# BAS @[[without T]] annotation syntax: negation type resolves via Expr::Call path.
# [without String] parses as Expr::Call { func: VarRef("without"), args: [String], implied: true } —
# NOT as Expr::Dict. This test exercises the Expr::Call arm in resolve_type_expr and the
# Expr::Call dispatch in resolve_annotation's PropertyDict branch.
# Type::Negation is conservative at runtime (always passes); 42 satisfies ~String.
[@[[without String]] 42]
=== out
Int(42)
